<title>UK: General Accident up to record on bid talk.</title>
<headline>General Accident up to record on bid talk.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in General Accident jumped to a record peak as bid rumours swirled around the sector, dealers said.</p>
<p>&quot;There is a feeling there is a deal to be done in the financial sector,&quot; said one dealer. &quot;There are continued murmurings that we are going to see a deal.&quot;</p>
<p>By 1020 GMT, the shares were up 23-1/2p to 773-1/2p, the day's best level.  </p>
<p>General Accident said it was not company policy to comment on market rumours.</p>
<p>-- Debra Sherman, London Newsroom +44 171 542 4026</p>
